{title: 373 - Seeking the Lost}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Church}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Ab]Seeking the lost, yes, kindly entreating
[Db]Wanderers on [Ab]the mountain astray;
[Eb]"Come unto Me," [Eb7]His [Ab]message repeating,
[Db]Words of the [Ab/Eb]Master [Eb7]speaking today.

Refrain:
[Db]Going afar (going afar)
[Db]Upon the [Ab]mountain (upon the [Eb7]mountain)
[Eb7]Bringing the wanderer [Cm]back again, back again,
[Db]Into the fold (into the fold)
[Ab]Of my Redeemer (of my Redeemer)
[Eb7]Jesus the Lamb [Cm]for [Ab]sinners slain, [Db/Ab]for [Ab]sinners slain.

Verse 2:
[Ab]Seeking the lost and pointing to [Db]Jesus
[Db]Souls that are weak [Ab]and hearts that are [Eb]sore,
[Eb]Leading them forth [Eb7]in [Ab]ways of salvation,
[Db]Showing the [Ab/Eb]path [Eb7]to life evermore.

Verse 3:
[Ab]Thus would I go on missions of [Db]mercy,
[Db]Following Christ [Ab]from day unto [Eb]day,
[Eb]Cheering the faint [Eb7]and [Ab]raising the fallen,
[Db]Pointing the [Ab/Eb]lost [Eb7]to Jesus, the [Ab]Way.
